{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20362",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 5.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Hi, um, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.85,
      "end_seconds": 10.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.79,
      "end_seconds": 19.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.02,
      "end_seconds": 23.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Alright, absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 28.52,
      "end_seconds": 37.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "Actually, it's sharp pain in the upper right of my tummy, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.72,
      "end_seconds": 41.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.54,
      "end_seconds": 46.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Around two weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 47.72,
      "end_seconds": 53.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Um, you know, I think it's been nearer three weeks, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.72,
      "end_seconds": 58.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.77,
      "end_seconds": 60.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.43,
      "end_seconds": 65.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Right, how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.2,
      "end_seconds": 72.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Actually, maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.63,
      "end_seconds": 76.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "What aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.18,
      "end_seconds": 81.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Fatty meals definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.46,
      "end_seconds": 88.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.16,
      "end_seconds": 94.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.24,
      "end_seconds": 98.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.64,
      "end_seconds": 120.5,
      "duration_seconds": 19.86,
      "text": "Let me think, when it starts I tend to get a bit of vomiting as well. The bit of vomiting? That's been for two weeks. With bit of vomiting, pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I'd say every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.32,
      "end_seconds": 126.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Any black stools, dark urine, fever or yellow eyes at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.52,
      "end_seconds": 137.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Okay, so no, no black stools, dark urine, fever or yellow eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.76,
      "end_seconds": 143.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Has there been any pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.98,
      "end_seconds": 151.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "No, no pale stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.87,
      "end_seconds": 155.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Right, is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.52,
      "end_seconds": 158.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.93,
      "end_seconds": 173.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.86,
      "end_seconds": 177.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.28,
      "end_seconds": 185.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.29,
      "end_seconds": 191.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.78,
      "end_seconds": 196.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.72,
      "end_seconds": 201.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I'm allergic to kiwi, I get an itchy mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.65,
      "end_seconds": 225.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Alright, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.18,
      "end_seconds": 243.74,
      "duration_seconds": 16.56,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.93,
      "end_seconds": 247.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.24,
      "end_seconds": 250.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.6,
      "end_seconds": 253.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.28,
      "end_seconds": 266.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.84,
      "end_seconds": 289.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 126 over 82, heart rate 78, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.71,
      "end_seconds": 295.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Ah, uh, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.67,
      "end_seconds": 300.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.58,
      "end_seconds": 306.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.24,
      "end_seconds": 320.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.21,
      "end_seconds": 323.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.59,
      "end_seconds": 344.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "There is tenderness under the right ribs when you breathe in, and no yellowing of the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.5,
      "end_seconds": 366.99,
      "duration_seconds": 17.49,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably biliary colic from gallstones. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Peptic ulcer is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.67,
      "end_seconds": 369.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.53,
      "end_seconds": 407.04,
      "duration_seconds": 35.51,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now biliary colic from gallstones is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'm sending you for liver blood tests because of upper abdominal pain. I'll start you on diclofenac, 50 milligrams, three times a day if needed, for three days. That should help with gallbladder pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Keep meals small and low in fat until we have the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.64,
      "end_seconds": 414.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Let's get you seen by the surgeons, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.83,
      "end_seconds": 421.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Could I get an ultrasound of the tummy done? A friend had it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.22,
      "end_seconds": 441.81,
      "duration_seconds": 18.59,
      "text": "Not right now, it wouldn't change what we do today. Come back or go to emergency straight away if you develop a fever, yellow eyes or severe constant pain. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.31,
      "end_seconds": 448.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}